nse of relationship:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong><i>Their</i></strong><i> sister is developing a web app. </i></p> <p><strong><i>Her</i></strong><i> professor is giving her some tips on how using HTLM tags. </i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>The following chart presents the <strong>possessive adjectives</strong> that we can use in English according to the subject pronouns:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject Pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possessive Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Our\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Their\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That way, if we want our title to have the biggest size, we need to put the heading between the tags. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The preformatted tag, < pre >content< /pre >, is an element that programmers can use when they want to keep the same format presented in their HTLM documents."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Examples of Commands for Basic Tags in HTML."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different types of <b>commands</b> that we can use when programming in HTML. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The chart below presents some commands for basic tags in HTML: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Category</span>  </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Commands</span>  </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Global </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< !--...-- >  <br /> < html >...< /html > <br /> < head >...< /head > <br /> < body >...< /body > <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Head </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< link > <br /> < meta > <br /> < base > <br /> < title >...< /title > <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Body </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< center >...< /center > <br /> < font size=# >...< /font > <br /> < b >...< /b > <br /> < cite >...< /cite > <br /> < h1 >...< /h1 > <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Lists</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< ul >...< /ul > <br /> < ol >...< /ol > <br /> < dl >...< /dl > <br /> < li > [...< /li >] <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Tables</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< table >...< /table > <br />\\t < caption >...< /caption > <br /> < tr >...< /tr > <br />\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Hypertext</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< a >...< /a > <br />\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tag"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a command that specifies the format of a webpage or application "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "noun "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This programming language works based on tags."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heading"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a title"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "noun"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That way, if we want our title to have the biggest size, we need to put the heading between the tags like this: < h1 >poems< /h1 >."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "format"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize written information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These elements can help defining the way a browser format and display the content of a page. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "empty "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without content"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some of the most common empty tags are < br/ > or < hr >. They are called this way because there is no need to put any content between them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "display"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show content on a website "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These elements can help defining the way a browser format and display the content of a page. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to permit something to happen "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All kind of documents even webpages start with headings, so this kind of tag enables to display them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think about a situation in which a friend needs some advice in the use of HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue where you give him/her some recommendations for building a good webpage. Don't forget to mention tags and using possessive pronouns properly. (no more than 200 words)."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Share your dialogue with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think about a situation in which a friend needs some advice in the  use of HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue where I give some recommendations for building a good webpage."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my dialogue with my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Teacher: </strong>Today, we are going to talk about basic tags in HTML. As you may know, HTLM is one of the most used markup languages in website or application developing.&nbsp; This programming language works based on tags; these elements can help defining the way a browser format and display the content of a page. Can you name some basic HTML tags?</p>\n<p><strong>Carl: </strong>Well, there are heading, paragraph, centering content, horizontal lines, preserve formatting, nonbreaking spaces, among other tags.</p>"}, {"time": "32500", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Teacher: </strong>That&rsquo;s right. Can you explain to us how heading tags work?</p>\n<p><strong>Carl: </strong>All kind of documents even webpages start with headings, so this kind of tag enables to display them. We can choose among six different levels of heading from &lt; h6 &gt; to &lt; h1 &gt; depending on the size we prefer for our heading. That way, if we want our title to have the biggest size, we need to put the heading between the tags like this: &lt; h1 &gt;poems&lt; /h1 &gt;.</p>\n<p><strong>Teacher: </strong>Good job Carl! As you mentioned before, there is also a tag to structure your texts by paragraphs. When you need it, you must use &lt; p &gt;for the opening and &lt; /p &gt; for the closing. But, in the case, you want to center your content, you have to use the centering content tag; it starts with &lt; center &gt; and closes with &lt; /center &gt;.</p>"}, {"time": "101500", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Carl: </strong>Can you give us some examples of empty elements?</p>\n<p><strong>Teacher: </strong>Sure. Some of the most common empty tags are &lt; br/ &gt; or &lt; hr &gt;. They are called this way because there is no need to put any content between them. &lt; br / &gt; or line break tag represents an empty element between lines,&nbsp; and &lt; hr &gt; or horizontal lines can be helpful to visualize the break-up sections of your page or application. Do you have any idea about when do we use preserve formatting?</p>\n<p><strong>Carl: </strong>The preformatted tag, &lt; pre &gt;content&lt; /pre &gt;, is an element that programmers can use when they want to keep the same format presented in their HTLM documents.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list the different types of basic tags in HTML. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about characteristics for different types of basic tags in HTML."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify commands for different types of basic tags in HTML."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think it is important to understand basic software terminologies when developing a website? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you know about programming in HTML?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "How can we add HTLM content when programming?"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Today, our class is about basic tags to program in HTML."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type"